  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Women-Owned Small Business (WOSB) set-aside obligations stand at $616M for FY2026 to date. The program recorded 2,055 awards with an average award size of $300K, and obligations fell 51.4% year over year. Prior fiscal years show substantially larger totals, including $1.3B in FY25 and FY24, $1.2B in FY23, $934M in FY22, and $856M in FY21. Department-level buying is concentrated: the Department of Defense obligated $306M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $81.8M, and the Department of Commerce obligated $50.9M in FY2026 to date. Other significant agency buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $39.1M and the Department of Justice at $23.7M. Industry concentration is focused in technical and professional services, led by Other Computer Related Services at $111M and Engineering Services at $110M. Top vendors are relatively small in absolute terms, led by INTELLECT SOLUTIONS, LLC at $18.5M and DTECHLOGIC LLC at $17.4M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to WOSB set-aside obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations for WOSB set-asides are $616M in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 51.4% year over year. Award activity produced 2,055 awards with an average award size of $300K. Fiscal-year history shows higher totals in prior years, with FY25 and FY24 each at $1.3B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is WOSB set-aside spending concentrated?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $306M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $81.8M and the Department of Commerce obligated $50.9M. Other concentrated industries include Other Computer Related Services at $111M and Engineering Services at $110M."
      }
    ]
  },
